Feridun delay is alone in a foreign land  his wife and child have already made it  to Germany he planned to follow them but  the pact between the EU and Turkey means  he's stuck in Istanbul even if he and  his friends make it to Greece the threat  of deportation looms large it's a  catastrophe not only for myself but for  those who have already reached Greece  they've risked everything to make it  this far there's nothing here for them  in Turkey the district of ax RI in  Istanbul normally the square is teeming  with migrants and the middlemen who  arranged their illegal passage to Greece  today the square is emptier than usual  demand for life vests for the perilous  sea crossing has dried up one angry  trader leaves his store and approaches  our camera his frustration is shared by  the migrants with their passage to  Western Europe effectively blocked they  don't know what to do next he is the  only one who will show us a way out of  this situation one possibility would be  through the new one-for-one program for  each Syrian returned to Turkey one will  be resettled in Europe but Fardeen de la  isn't hopeful they'll take in 70,000 of  us but I don't expect to be amongst them  they'll likely take those in the refugee  camps or those registered by the United  Nations anyone waiting to be reunited  with their family like me he and his  friends can do is wait and hope
 

